  "description": "The basement is organised as a sequence of ancillary spaces, comprising a cinema room, wine cellar and pantry, supported by general storage and a utility area. A WC is positioned beneath the stair.\nAt ground-floor level, the former lobby is reconfigured to provide a bathroom and boot room. The remaining accommodation is divided into two separate rooms: a small kitchen and an independent gym. Internal access to the basement is retained, with the internal spiral staircase. \nThe first floor accommodates two bedrooms arranged off the landing and served by a shared WC.\nThe second floor comprises a living room with an adjoining office space, together with a WC, establishing a distinct upper-level zone separate from the service and ancillary functions below.\n\n",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "3 YEAR CONSENT PERIOD: The development hereby permitted shall be begun not later than the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\n\r\nREASON: To comply with the provisions of Section 91(1)(a) of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 as amended by the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004 (Chapter 5)."
